<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
  <title>QuantLens Validation Battery v2 Report</title>
  <style>
    :root{--ink:#102a36;--soft:#526873;--line:#dbe4e8;--panel:#f6f9fa;--teal:#087f7a;--warn:#8a5200;--bad:#a4262c}
    *{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#fff;color:var(--ink);font:15px/1.55 system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif}
    main{max-width:1050px;margin:auto;padding:40px 28px 70px}h1{font-size:2.15rem;line-height:1.15;margin:.2rem 0}h2{margin-top:2.4rem;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:1.2rem}h3{margin-bottom:.35rem}.eyebrow{color:var(--teal);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}.muted{color:var(--soft)}
    .banner{padding:16px 18px;border-left:5px solid var(--teal);background:var(--panel);margin:22px 0}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(190px,1fr));gap:12px}.card{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:15px;background:#fff}.metric{font-size:1.45rem;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;font-weight:750}.status-PASS{color:var(--teal)}.status-FAIL{color:var(--bad)}.status-INCONCLUSIVE{color:var(--warn)}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}th,td{padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);text-align:left;vertical-align:top}code{font-size:.88em;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.chart{overflow:auto}.finding{margin:12px 0;padding:16px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px}.disclosure{margin-top:30px;padding:16px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--panel)}
    @media print{main{max-width:none;padding:0}.card,.finding{break-inside:avoid}}
  </style>
</head>
<body><main>
  {% set is_user_uploaded = manifest.data_label == 'USER_UPLOADED' %}
  {% set is_licensed = manifest.data_label == 'LICENSED_PROVIDER' %}
  {# Absent provenance resolves to Undefined here, which compares false, so a run on
     the synthetic fixture keeps the price-return wording it has always had. #}
  {% set is_total_return =
       data_provenance.price_adjustment == 'operator_attested_total_return_ohlc' %}
  {# Only the bundle seeder writes an operator-attested basis, so this is the honest
     discriminator between data QuantLens shipped and data the reader imported. #}
  {% set is_operator_bundle = is_user_uploaded and is_total_return %}
  {# Every metric label follows the basis too, not only the return-basis paragraphs.
     A tile reading "price return" over a dividend-adjusted series names the wrong
     quantity in the first number a reader looks at, and this document used to state
     one basis in §1 and the other in §7 and the tiles. #}
  {% set basis_term = 'total return' if is_total_return else 'price return' %}
  {% set Basis_term = 'Total return' if is_total_return else 'Price return' %}
  {% if research_mode == 'sandbox' %}
  <div class="banner"><strong>Sandbox test evidence — non-formal.</strong>
    This run used the separate development allowance. It is not formal research
    evidence and did not access the Strict-validation final holdout.</div>
  {% endif %}
  {% if artifact_contract and not artifact_contract.verified_financial_semantics %}
  <div class="banner"><strong>Original historical evidence contract.</strong>
    This report is reproduced under <code>{{ artifact_contract.ledger_semantics_version }}</code>
    and <code>{{ artifact_contract.execution_semantics_version }}</code>. The configured
    <code>slippage_bps</code> value is legacy linear execution friction, not an adverse
    effective fill price. These results are displayable but are not eligible for
    metrics-v2, contract-gated comparison, ranking, or Research Copilot claims.</div>
  {% endif %}
  <p class="eyebrow">Validation Battery v2 · deterministic server report</p>
  <h1>{{ spec.universe.symbol }} locked-rule validation</h1>
  <p class="muted">Run <code>{{ manifest.manifest_id }}</code> · {{ manifest.data_label }} · {{ manifest.created_at }}</p>

  <div class="banner">
    {% if battery_status == 'PASS' %}
      <strong class="status-PASS">Development audit complete — no declared fragility trigger fired.</strong>
    {% elif battery_status == 'FAIL' %}
      <strong class="status-FAIL">Development audit detected a declared fragility.</strong>
    {% else %}
      <strong class="status-INCONCLUSIVE">Development audit is inconclusive.</strong>
    {% endif %}
    Technical battery status: <code>{{ battery_status }}</code>. This status covers
    development positive-fold coverage, development cost stress, and regime sample
    coverage; it does <strong>not</strong> grade final-holdout performance or approve a
    strategy for investment. The access-controlled final holdout is shown separately as
    primary evidence and was evaluated once at declared base costs only.
  </div>
  {# The basis follows the data, not the other way round. Stating price return over a
     dividend-adjusted series tells a reader their real return would have been higher
     than shown, when the dividends are already inside these figures. #}
  {% if is_total_return %}
  <p class="muted"><strong>Return basis:</strong> total return; dividends and
    distributions are reinvested in the underlying series. These figures therefore
    approximate the full investor holding-period return before tax.</p>
  {% else %}
  <p class="muted"><strong>Return basis:</strong> split-adjusted price return; dividends
    and distributions are excluded. These figures do not represent the full investor
    holding-period return.</p>
  {% endif %}
  <p>{{ restatement }}</p>

  <h2>1 · Data source and return basis</h2>
  <div class="card">
    {% if is_operator_bundle %}
      {# The operator-attested basis is written only by the bundle seeder, so it is what
         separates data QuantLens supplied from data the reader brought. Saying
         "user-provided" here would credit the reader for bytes they never chose, and
         CC BY 4.0 makes the credit below a condition of shipping them at all. #}
      <p><strong>Bundled historical observations supplied by QuantLens.</strong> These
      bars were not provided by you. QuantLens checked structure, chronology and hashes
      and sealed them, but did not independently authenticate the upstream source or its
      corporate-action accuracy.</p>
      <p class="muted">Elkassabgi, A. (2026). <em>HF Data Library: Free 1-Minute Intraday
      U.S. Equity Data.</em> Zenodo, doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19501605 — licensed CC BY 4.0
      (creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/); pre-March-2022 bars derive from PiTrading
      via the consolidated tape (CTA/UTP). Coverage ends 2022-03-04, where that licence
      ends; this is historical data and not a live market feed.</p>
    {% elif is_user_uploaded %}
      <p><strong>User-provided daily observations.</strong> QuantLens checked structure,
      chronology, hashes, and declared adjustment metadata, but did not independently
      authenticate the source or corporate-action accuracy.</p>
    {% elif is_licensed %}
      <p><strong>Licensed-provider daily observations.</strong>
      {{ data_provenance.required_attribution | default('', true) }}</p>
      <p class="muted">Provider {{ data_provenance.provider_id }} · feed
      {{ data_provenance.feed }} · MIC {{ data_provenance.mic }} · retrieved
      {{ data_provenance.retrieved_at }}</p>
    {% else %}
      <p><strong>Bundled synthetic fixture — not market data.</strong> Results from this
      source are suitable only for workflow testing and cannot support a market or
      investment conclusion.</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if is_total_return %}
    <p><strong>Return basis:</strong> total return. Dividends and distributions are
    reinvested in the underlying series, so these figures approximate the full investor
    holding-period return before tax. Uninvested cash earns 0% in the current engine;
    Sharpe also uses rf = 0.</p>
    {% else %}
    <p><strong>Return basis:</strong> split-adjusted price return. Dividends and
    distributions are excluded, so these figures are not total investor holding-period
    returns. Uninvested cash earns 0% in the current engine; Sharpe also uses rf = 0.</p>
    {% endif %}
    <p class="muted">Requested window: {{ spec.data.range.start }} →
    {{ spec.data.range.end }} · snapshot <code>{{ snapshot.snapshot_id }}</code> ·
    snapshot SHA-256 <code>{{ snapshot.sha256 }}</code></p>
  </div>

  <h2>2 · Primary evidence</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card"><div class="muted">Development strategy {{ basis_term }}</div><div class="metric">{{ development_result.strategy_metrics.total_return | default(none, true) | pct }}</div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="muted">Development benchmark {{ basis_term }}</div><div class="metric">{{ development_result.benchmark_metrics.total_return | default(none, true) | pct }}</div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="muted">Final primary return ({{ basis_term }} basis)</div><div class="metric">{{ final_result.strategy_metrics.total_return | default(none, true) | pct }}</div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="muted">Final benchmark {{ basis_term }}</div><div class="metric">{{ final_result.benchmark_metrics.total_return | default(none, true) | pct }}</div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="muted">Final strategy max drawdown</div><div class="metric">{{ final_result.strategy_metrics.max_drawdown | default(none, true) | pct }}</div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="muted">Final benchmark max drawdown</div><div class="metric">{{ final_result.benchmark_metrics.max_drawdown | default(none, true) | pct }}</div></div>
  </div>
  <p class="muted">Final execution count: {{ final_audit.primary_evaluation_count }} · final cost multiplier: 1.0× · locked rule hash: <code>{{ final_audit.execution_binding.locked_rule_sha256 }}</code></p>
  <h3>Development segment</h3>
  <div class="chart">{{ development_chart | safe }}</div>
  <h3>Final-holdout segment</h3>
  <div class="chart">{{ final_chart | safe }}</div>
  <p class="muted">Development and final holdout are independent simulations with
  separate initial-capital bases. Their endpoints are intentionally not connected.</p>

  <table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Metric</th><th scope="col">Development strategy</th><th scope="col">Development benchmark</th><th scope="col">Final strategy</th><th scope="col">Final benchmark</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><th scope="row">{{ Basis_term }}</th><td>{{ development_result.strategy_metrics.total_return | default(none, true) | pct }}</td><td>{{ development_result.benchmark_metrics.total_return | default(none, true) | pct }}</td><td>{{ final_result.strategy_metrics.total_return | default(none, true) | pct }}</td><td>{{ final_result.benchmark_metrics.total_return | default(none, true) | pct }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">CAGR</th><td>{{ development_result.strategy_metrics.cagr | default(none, true) | pct }}</td><td>{{ development_result.benchmark_metrics.cagr | default(none, true) | pct }}</td><td>{{ final_result.strategy_metrics.cagr | default(none, true) | pct }}</td><td>{{ final_result.benchmark_metrics.cagr | default(none, true) | pct }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Sharpe (rf = 0)</th><td>{{ development_result.strategy_metrics.sharpe | default(none, true) | num }}</td><td>{{ development_result.benchmark_metrics.sharpe | default(none, true) | num }}</td><td>{{ final_result.strategy_metrics.sharpe | default(none, true) | num }}</td><td>{{ final_result.benchmark_metrics.sharpe | default(none, true) | num }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Max drawdown</th><td>{{ development_result.strategy_metrics.max_drawdown | default(none, true) | pct }}</td><td>{{ development_result.benchmark_metrics.max_drawdown | default(none, true) | pct }}</td><td>{{ final_result.strategy_metrics.max_drawdown | default(none, true) | pct }}</td><td>{{ final_result.benchmark_metrics.max_drawdown | default(none, true) | pct }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Costs paid</th><td>{{ development_result.strategy_metrics.total_costs | default(none, true) | money }}</td><td>{{ development_result.benchmark_metrics.total_costs | default(none, true) | money }}</td><td>{{ final_result.strategy_metrics.total_costs | default(none, true) | money }}</td><td>{{ final_result.benchmark_metrics.total_costs | default(none, true) | money }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Time in market</th><td>{{ development_result.strategy_metrics.exposure | default(none, true) | pct }}</td><td>{{ development_result.benchmark_metrics.exposure | default(none, true) | pct }}</td><td>{{ final_result.strategy_metrics.exposure | default(none, true) | pct }}</td><td>{{ final_result.benchmark_metrics.exposure | default(none, true) | pct }}</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>

  <h2>3 · Development walk-forward: positive-fold coverage</h2>
  <p>This section uses development observations only. The rule is fixed across every
  expanding fold. The declared check asks whether at least half of folds have a positive
  absolute {{ basis_term }}; it does not test benchmark outperformance or economic magnitude.
  Its sealed technical check id is <code>walk_forward_stability</code> (walk forward stability).</p>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card"><div class="muted">Fold count</div><div class="metric">{{ walk_forward.fold_count }}</div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="muted">Positive-fold ratio</div><div class="metric">{{ walk_forward.positive_fold_ratio | default(none, true) | pct }}</div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="muted">Median fold Sharpe</div><div class="metric">{{ walk_forward.median_fold_sharpe | default(none, true) | num }}</div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="muted">Worst fold {{ basis_term }}</div><div class="metric">{{ walk_forward.worst_fold_return | default(none, true) | pct }}</div></div>
  </div>

  <h2>4 · Development-only cost stress</h2>
  <p>No stressed case below reads or recomputes the final holdout.</p>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Declared-cost multiple</th><th>Development {{ basis_term }}</th><th>Development Sharpe</th><th>Development costs</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  {% for row in development_cost_stress.rows %}
    <tr><td>{{ row.multiplier }}×</td><td>{{ row.development.total_return | default(none, true) | pct }}</td><td>{{ row.development.sharpe | default(none, true) | num }}</td><td>{{ row.development.total_costs | default(none, true) | money }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody></table>

  <h2>5 · Preregistered findings</h2>
  {% for f in findings %}
  <section class="finding">
    <h3 class="status-{{ f.status }}">{{ f.status_icon }} {% if f.id == 'walk_forward_stability' %}positive-fold coverage{% else %}{{ f.id | replace('_',' ') }}{% endif %}</h3>
    <p>{{ f.summary }}</p>
    {% if f.id == 'walk_forward_stability' %}
      <p>Development folds: {{ f.evidence.fold_count }} · positive ratio: {{ f.evidence.positive_fold_ratio | default(none, true) | pct }} · worst {{ basis_term }}: {{ f.evidence.worst_fold_return | default(none, true) | pct }}</p>
    {% elif f.id == 'development_cost_fragility' %}
      <p>Development 1× {{ basis_term }}: {{ f.evidence.base.development.total_return | default(none, true) | pct }} · development 2× {{ basis_term }}: {{ f.evidence.doubled.development.total_return | default(none, true) | pct }}</p>
    {% elif f.id == 'regime_coverage' %}
      <p>Preregistered minimum: {{ validation_plan.regime_law.minimum_observations }} observations per state.</p>
      <ul>{% for state in f.evidence.states %}<li>{{ state.regime }}: {{ state.observations }} ({{ state.status }})</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
      <p class="muted">This finding checks sample coverage only; it does not establish
      positive or stable performance inside a regime.</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% endfor %}

  <h2>6 · Validation design and integrity</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Rule policy: locked; no parameter search or selection.</li>
    <li>Walk-forward: expanding fixed rule; standard test window {{ validation_plan.test_window_bars }} bars.</li>
    <li>Final holdout: access-controlled, single-use capability at declared base costs.</li>
    <li>Research-agent scope: development evidence only.</li>
  </ul>
  <details><summary>Technical audit index</summary><ul>{% for e in ledger.entries %}<li><code>{{ e.kind }}</code> · <code>{{ e.sha256 }}</code> · <code>{{ e.producer }}</code></li>{% endfor %}</ul></details>

  <h2>7 · Production limitations</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The final holdout uses a one-time in-process capability and cross-run reveal ledger. It is not yet isolated under an independent OS principal or object-store ACL.</li>
    <li>The control-plane anchor is write-once in the local database but is not yet protected by a production MAC or immutable external store.</li>
    {% if is_total_return %}
    <li>Returns are total returns: dividends and distributions are reinvested in the
    underlying series, so they are already inside every figure above and must not be
    added to them.</li>
    {% else %}
    <li>Returns are split-adjusted price returns. Dividends and distributions are
    excluded; this can materially change both strategy and benchmark outcomes.</li>
    {% endif %}
    <li>Uninvested cash earns 0% and Sharpe uses rf = 0. Long cash periods therefore do
    not include the return an investor might earn on cash or Treasury bills.</li>
    <li>Commission and slippage are constant bps assumptions. Backtests exclude dynamic
    bid–ask spreads, liquidity, capacity, market impact, borrowing, taxes, and future
    regime changes.</li>
    <li>The battery status does not apply an investment objective to final-holdout
    returns and must not be interpreted as strategy approval.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="disclosure"><strong>Standing disclosure.</strong> This is research evidence, not investment advice, a forecast, or a recommendation to trade.</div>
</main></body></html>
